Good morrow,

The council sat this morning touching the coronation arrangements. Opinions w=
ere divided, but the King's will carried the day.

I trust this note finds you all in one piece.

With all due reverence,
Sir Henry Norris

--
Sent from my writing-desk. Pray excuse any brevity or blots.
